From 5c88c1d6eaca7d28b32e2d8d796a397a9f41a3db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gavin John <gavinnjohn@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 21:55:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 23/28] demux: avformat: fix container origin handling in
 DEMUX_SET_TIME

DEMUX_SET_TIME passed the seek target to av_seek_frame() as
"i64 + i_start_time", leaving i64 itself zero based, but then still
handed "i64 - i_start_time" to ResetTime(). The subtraction has no
matching addition, so the value given to ResetTime() is short by the
container origin. Its two siblings, DEMUX_SET_POSITION and
DEMUX_SET_SEEKPOINT, are correct precisely because their i64 does
carry the origin.

The origin used to be folded into i64 up front, so the subtraction was
right; 0c8fe7c6b5 dropped that assignment and moved the origin into the
av_seek_frame() argument without touching the ResetTime() call, and
929f09bfc0 then moved TO_AV_TS() onto the va_arg.

ResetTime() must be given a zero based timestamp: Demux() rebases every
frame by start_time, so that is the timeline the demuxer emits.

This only shows up where avformat reports a non-zero start_time, which
is routine for MPEG-TS/PS and some MXF and RTP captures, and is why it
went unnoticed on MP4 and MKV. Seeking past the origin sets
ES_OUT_SET_NEXT_DISPLAY_TIME start_time too early, so a precise seek
quietly degrades to the preceding keyframe and DEMUX_GET_TIME reads low
until the first PCR corrects it. Seeking below the origin makes the
argument negative, ResetTime() takes its i_time < 0 path and issues no
ES_OUT_SET_NEXT_DISPLAY_TIME at all, losing precise seeking entirely -
for a stream starting at 10s, that is every seek into the first 10s.

Add the origin into i64 up front instead, so all three cases read
identically and the debug message reports the timestamp actually sought.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 modules/demux/avformat/demux.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/modules/demux/avformat/demux.c b/modules/demux/avformat/demux.c
index 0a4cfbdca3..1de47aeeca 100644
--- a/modules/demux/avformat/demux.c
+++ b/modules/demux/avformat/demux.c
@@ -1170,12 +1170,12 @@ static int Control( demux_t *p_demux, int i_query, va_list args )
 
         case DEMUX_SET_TIME:
         {
-            i64 = TO_AV_TS(va_arg( args, vlc_tick_t ));
+            i64 = TO_AV_TS(va_arg( args, vlc_tick_t )) + i_start_time;
             bool precise = va_arg( args, int );
 
             msg_Warn( p_demux, "DEMUX_SET_TIME: %"PRId64, i64 );
 
-            if( av_seek_frame( p_sys->ic, -1, i64 + i_start_time, AVSEEK_FLAG_BACKWARD ) < 0 )
+            if( av_seek_frame( p_sys->ic, -1, i64, AVSEEK_FLAG_BACKWARD ) < 0 )
             {
                 return VLC_EGENERIC;
             }
